<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The launcher icon foreground: the whole VorldX Saarthi logo — the mark, the
  "VorldX Saarthi" wordmark and the MANAGE · TRACK · MOVE · TOGETHER strapline —
  the same `brand_lockup` the splash and welcome screens show.

  ## Fitting it to every launcher's mask

  The box matches the artwork's own 900:813 proportions, so the drawable fills
  it without stretching. 44dp wide, well inside the 66dp safe circle, because
  some launchers mask far more than the standard: on a Redmi with HyperOS a 54dp
  logo lost the pin, both ends of "VorldX" and the strapline to the squircle.

  A `<bitmap>` rather than the drawable directly, for `mipMap`: the 900px
  artwork is drawn at a sixth of its size here, and sampling it down without
  mipmaps is what turns the strapline into noise.

  The file lives in `drawable-nodpi` so it is never pre-scaled by density
  before being drawn back down.
-->
<layer-list xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android">
    <item
        android:gravity="center"
        android:width="44dp"
        android:height="40dp">
        <bitmap
            android:src="@drawable/brand_lockup"
            android:gravity="fill"
            android:filter="true"
            android:mipMap="true" />
    </item>
</layer-list>
